// Rules whose totals under logical compute units depend on the memo policy counts of calls that
// dispatch guards skip (bench/logical_exact_test.go). Each "c" is a position where u's guard skips
// a call of the memoized rule word, which counts a call of word without a repeat. Each word is
// called twice at its position (by u, then by item), a repeat; word becomes eager, and its second
// call a memo hit that counts 1 unit instead of the length of the word, once repeats exceed a
// sixteenth of its calls. The skipped calls therefore decide where that happens.
package policy

@start
rule doc = (u / item)* $$
rule u = word "!" / "c"
rule item = word "." / "b"
rule word = "a" tail
rule tail = [a-z]*
